      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Car Transportation In Tadpatri</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">
	<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">During the destination delivery handover process for automobiles and cars, it is essential to ensure a thorough examination of the vehicle prior to accepting it for delivery to the intended recipient.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This comprehensive handover process involves conducting a daylight re-inspection, verifying the odometer reading against the LR bill of lading, and obtaining a signed condition sign-off from the receiving party.</span></li></ul>

	<h3>Daylight Condition Re-inspection</h3>
	<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 01</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Examine the vehicle under daylight conditions to ensure there have been no damages or modifications during transportation.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 02</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Check for scratches, dents, dings, or any other visible signs of damage.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 03</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Investigate any areas that may be difficult to see during the initial inspection, such as under the hood, engine compartment, and trunk.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 04</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Document any noticeable imperfections or discrepancies in the inspection report.</p>
  </div>
</div>

	<h3>Odometer Verification</h3>
	<p>Verify the vehicle's odometer reading against the provided LR bill of lading:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Obtain the odometer reading from the vehicle.</li>
		<li>Compare the odometer reading to the information listed on the LR bill of lading, ensuring they match.</li>
		<li>If the readings differ, consult the transportation company or shipper to resolve any discrepancies.</li>
		<li>Document the verification process and any differences in the inspection report for future reference.</li>
</ul>

	<h3>Signed Condition Sign-off</h3>
	<p>Upon confirming the vehicle's condition and verifying the odometer reading, proceed to obtain a signed condition sign-off from the receiving party:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Provide a comprehensive inspection report detailing the vehicle's condition and any visible damages.</li>
		<li>Ask the receiving party to review and confirm the condition of the vehicle.</li>
		<li>Ask the receiving party to sign the inspection report, acknowledging their acceptance of the vehicle's current condition.</li>
		<li>Gather a copy of the signed inspection report for your records, ensuring a clear record of the vehicle's condition upon delivery.</li>
</ul>

	<p>By conducting a thorough daylight re-inspection, verifying the odometer reading, and ensuring a signed condition sign-off, you can provide a guarantee of the vehicle's condition upon delivery to the recipient.</p>

	<p>It is essential to document all findings and inspections thoroughly to provide transparency and preserve your credibility as a delivery handler. This meticulous approach ensures a smoother coordination between the sender, transportation company, and the recipient, fostering trust and opening opportunities for future collaborations.</p>

	<p>Upon completing these steps, the recipient will have a clear understanding of the vehicle's condition, allowing for a seamless handover and minimizing potential disputes or issues later on.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



